      "receiptSource": "Original Receipt in \u0027\u003Ci\u003EEnglish Housewifry\u003C/i\u003E\u0027 by Elizabeth Moxon, 1764 (\u003Ca href=\u0022references.html#moxon-1764\u0022\u003E\u003Cb\u003EMoxon 1764\u003C/b\u003E\u003C/a\u003E)",
      "receiptText": "\u003Cb\u003E333. To make CORDIAL WATER of COWSLIPS.\u003C/b\u003E\u003Cbr\u003E\nTake two quarts of cowslip peeps, a slip of balm, two sprigs of rosemary, a stick of cinnamon, half an orange peel, half a lemon peel, a pint of brandy, and a pint of ale; lay all these to steep twelve hours, then distil them on a cold still.\u003Cbr\u003E"
